    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d827">

                <pb facs="0771" n="759" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg759"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Files of the Division of Middle Eastern Affairs:
                    Lot 57–D178</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Telephone Conversation, by the Secretary
                        of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-12-30">December 30, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Lord Halifax telephoned me this morning and during the course of our conversation
                    I mentioned to him the disappointment which we had felt to learn that the
                    British Minister to Saudi Arabia, Mr. <pb facs="0772" n="760" xml:id="pg760"/>
                    Jordan, had been returned to his post.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d827-f1"/> The
                    Ambassador seemed to understand and asked if I would leave it in his hands.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E[<hi rendition="#small-caps">dward</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >tettinius</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d827-f1" n="90" xml:id="d827-f1-content">
                <p>Minister Jordan, who had been on leave, returned to Jidda about mid-November.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
